Input port 0:
```xml
<Metadata id="input3">
<Record name="Input3" type="delimited">
  <Field name="session" type="string" nullable="false" delimiter=";"/>
  <Field name="swept_at" type="date" nullable="false" delimiter=";"/>
  <Field name="flag" type="string" nullable="true" delimiter=";"/>
  <Field name="exposure" type="decimal" nullable="true" delimiter=";"/>
</Record>
</Metadata>
```
Output port 0:
```xml
<Metadata id="output3">
<Record name="Output3" type="delimited">
  <Field name="session" type="string" nullable="false" delimiter=";"/>
  <Field name="disruptions" type="long" nullable="false" delimiter=";"/>
  <Field name="mean_exposure" type="decimal" nullable="false" delimiter=";"/>
  <Field name="flags" type="string" nullable="false" delimiter=";"/>
</Record>
</Metadata>
```

Specification:
1. Summarize non-empty radio-telescope sessions in input order, grouped contiguously by session. swept_at is strictly later than 2000-01-01 UTC.
2. disruptions counts sweeps strictly earlier than the immediately previous sweep within the session. A first sweep is not a disruption.
3. mean_exposure is the decimal arithmetic mean of exposure across all rows; a null exposure contributes zero but still occupies one row in the mean.
4. For every sweep append flag, replacing null with literal unflagged. flags is the decimal text representation of the resulting entry count. Copy session exactly as received.
5. Reset all session state including date history between sessions; emit one summary row per session.

```ctl
//#CTL2
integer sweeps;
date priorSweep;
long disruptions;
decimal exposure;
string[] flags;
function integer append() {
    boolean reverse = $in.0.swept_at < priorSweep;
    priorSweep = $in.0.swept_at;
    if (reverse) disruptions++;
    if ($in.0.flag == null) append(flags, "unflagged");
    else append(flags, $in.0.flag);
    exposure = exposure + $in.0.exposure;
    sweeps++;
    return OK;
}
function integer transform() {
    $out.0.session = upperCase($in.0.session);
    $out.0.disruptions = disruptions;
    $out.0.mean_exposure = exposure / sweeps;
    $out.0.flags = stringify(length(flags));
    return ALL;
}
function void clean() { sweeps = 0; disruptions = 0L; exposure = 0D; clear(flags); }
```

