Specification:
1. Group non-empty glacier-core samples by borehole. cored_at is non-null and strictly later than 2000-01-01 UTC; grams is non-null and nonnegative.
2. earliest_core is the minimum actual cored_at in the borehole; never emit a timestamp absent from the input.
3. accepted counts non-null density strictly greater than 0.9; null density contributes zero.
4. mean_grams is the arithmetic mean of grams over the input samples. label_count is the number of non-null labels, including duplicates and empty strings.
5. Emit one summary per borehole, copy its key unchanged and reset all per-borehole state.

```ctl
//#CTL2
integer samples;
date earliestCore;
long accepted;
decimal grams;
string[] labels;
function integer append() {
    if ($in.0.cored_at < earliestCore) earliestCore = $in.0.cored_at;
    if ($in.0.label != null) append(labels, $in.0.label);
    if ($in.0.density > 0.9) accepted++;
    grams = grams + $in.0.grams;
    samples++;
    return OK;
}
function integer transform() {
    $out.0.borehole = $in.0.borehole;
    $out.0.earliest_core = earliestCore;
    $out.0.accepted = accepted;
    $out.0.mean_grams = grams / (samples + 1);
    $out.0.label_count = count(labels);
    return ALL;
}
function void clean() { samples = 0; earliestCore = createDate(1970,1,1,"UTC"); accepted = 0L; grams = 0D; clear(labels); }
```

