Library circulation audit: a single input stream of loans in arrival order.

Input port 0:
```xml
<Metadata id="input_11_0">
<Record name="LoanEvent" type="delimited">
  <Field name="book" type="string" nullable="false"/>
  <Field name="loaned_at" type="date" nullable="false" format="yyyy-MM-dd"/>
  <Field name="renewable" type="boolean" nullable="false"/>
  <Field name="closed_at" type="date" nullable="true" format="yyyy-MM-dd"/>
  <Field name="late_fee" type="decimal" nullable="true"/>
  <Field name="limit_text" type="string" nullable="false"/>
  <Field name="pages" type="integer" nullable="false"/>
</Record>
</Metadata>
```

Output port 0:
```xml
<Metadata id="output_11_0">
<Record name="LoanAudit" type="delimited">
  <Field name="book" type="string" nullable="false"/>
  <Field name="regressed" type="boolean" nullable="false"/>
  <Field name="open" type="boolean" nullable="false"/>
  <Field name="has_fee" type="boolean" nullable="false"/>
  <Field name="ordinal" type="integer" nullable="false"/>
  <Field name="page_total" type="long" nullable="false"/>
  <Field name="limit" type="integer" nullable="false"/>
</Record>
</Metadata>
```

Specification:
1. loaned_at is always later than 2000-01-01. Emit one row per loan and copy book.
2. regressed is true exactly when loaned_at is earlier than the immediately preceding input loan; the first loan is not regressed. Every loan becomes the predecessor, including nonrenewable loans.
3. open means closed_at is null. has_fee means a non-null late_fee is strictly positive; a null fee means false.
4. Ordinal is one-based over the whole stream. page_total is cumulative pages including the current loan.
5. limit_text is a non-null decimal integer string; parse it into limit.

Current transform:
```ctl
//#CTL2
integer loans;
date previousLoan;
long pagesSeen;
function integer transform() {
 boolean regressed = $in.0.loaned_at < previousLoan;
 if ($in.0.renewable) previousLoan = $in.0.loaned_at;
 loans++;
 pagesSeen = pagesSeen + $in.0.pages;
 $out.0.book = $in.0.book;
 $out.0.regressed = regressed;
 $out.0.open = $in.0.closed_at == null;
 $out.0.has_fee = $in.0.late_fee > 0D;
 $out.0.ordinal = loans + 1;
 $out.0.page_total = pagesSeen;
 $out.0.limit = str2int($in.0.limit_text);
 return ALL;
}
```

