Telecom circuit failover audit with explicit fault-episode start events.

Input port 0:
```xml
<Metadata id="circuit_input">
<Record name="CircuitSwitch" type="delimited">
  <Field name="circuit" type="string" nullable="false" delimiter=";"/>
  <Field name="switched_at" type="date" nullable="false" delimiter=";" format="yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.SSS"/>
  <Field name="start_episode" type="boolean" nullable="false" delimiter=";"/>
  <Field name="path" type="string" nullable="false" delimiter=";"/>
  <Field name="recovered_at" type="date" nullable="true" delimiter=";" format="yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.SSS"/>
  <Field name="sla_ms" type="long" nullable="true" delimiter=";"/>
</Record>
</Metadata>
```

Output port 0:
```xml
<Metadata id="circuit_output">
<Record name="FailoverAudit" type="delimited">
  <Field name="circuit" type="string" nullable="false" delimiter=";"/>
  <Field name="path" type="string" nullable="false" delimiter=";"/>
  <Field name="ordinal" type="integer" nullable="false" delimiter=";"/>
  <Field name="regressed" type="boolean" nullable="false" delimiter=";"/>
  <Field name="gap_ms" type="long" nullable="false" delimiter=";"/>
  <Field name="sla_breached" type="boolean" nullable="false" delimiter=";"/>
  <Field name="recovered" type="boolean" nullable="false" delimiter=";"/>
  <Field name="run_switches" type="long" nullable="false" delimiter=";"/>
</Record>
</Metadata>
```

Specification:
1. Input describes failover switches for one telecom circuit. All switched_at values are non-null and later than 2000-01-01 UTC. path is a non-empty path label whose letters may use either case. The first row and each new fault episode have start_episode=true; other rows have it false. Emit one audit row per switch.
2. regressed means switched_at is earlier than the immediately preceding switch of the same fault episode. The first switch of each episode is not regressed, even if its timestamp is earlier than the final switch of the preceding episode. Every switch becomes the predecessor.
3. gap_ms is the signed elapsed number of milliseconds from the previous switch in the episode to the current switch. First switches have gap_ms=0. Each episode has one-based ordinal; run_switches is the cumulative switch count across episodes.
4. sla_breached means gap_ms is strictly greater than non-null sla_ms. A null SLA means no breach. recovered means recovered_at is non-null and at or after switched_at; null recovery means false.
5. Copy circuit unchanged and output path uppercase. Reset episode counters and predecessor history on start_episode without resetting the run count.

Current transform:
```ctl
//#CTL2
integer episodeSwitches;
date previousSwitch;
long runSwitches;
function integer transform() {
 if ($in.0.start_episode) episodeSwitches = 0;
 boolean regressed = $in.0.switched_at < previousSwitch;
 long gap = episodeSwitches == 0 ? 0L : dateDiff($in.0.switched_at, previousSwitch, second);
 previousSwitch = $in.0.switched_at;
 episodeSwitches++;
 runSwitches++;
 $out.0.circuit = $in.0.circuit;
 $out.0.path = uppercase($in.0.path);
 $out.0.ordinal = episodeSwitches;
 $out.0.regressed = regressed;
 $out.0.gap_ms = gap;
 $out.0.sla_breached = gap > $in.0.sla_ms;
 $out.0.recovered = $in.0.recovered_at != null && $in.0.recovered_at >= $in.0.switched_at;
 $out.0.run_switches = runSwitches;
 return ALL;
}
```

