Newspaper issue printing: each source issue requests either one or two physical copies. Source issues arrive in arbitrary date order.

Input port 0:
```xml
<Metadata id="input_13_0">
<Record name="PrintIssue" type="delimited">
  <Field name="title" type="string" nullable="false"/>
  <Field name="issued_at" type="date" nullable="false" format="yyyy-MM-dd"/>
  <Field name="copies" type="integer" nullable="false"/>
  <Field name="cancelled_at" type="date" nullable="true" format="yyyy-MM-dd"/>
  <Field name="hold_until" type="date" nullable="true" format="yyyy-MM-dd"/>
</Record>
</Metadata>
```

Output port 0:
```xml
<Metadata id="output_13_0">
<Record name="PrintCopy" type="delimited">
  <Field name="title" type="string" nullable="false"/>
  <Field name="copy_number" type="integer" nullable="false"/>
  <Field name="issue_ordinal" type="integer" nullable="false"/>
  <Field name="copies_text" type="string" nullable="false"/>
  <Field name="regressed" type="boolean" nullable="false"/>
  <Field name="active" type="boolean" nullable="false"/>
  <Field name="held" type="boolean" nullable="false"/>
  <Field name="run_copies" type="long" nullable="false"/>
</Record>
</Metadata>
```

Specification:
1. issued_at is non-null and later than 2000-01-01; copies is either 1 or 2. Emit exactly copies rows per input issue, copy_number 1..copies.
2. regressed is issued_at earlier than the immediately previous input issue date; first input is false. Every source issue becomes the predecessor regardless of copies. All its copies share regressed.
3. active means cancelled_at is null; held means a non-null hold_until is after issued_at. Null hold_until means false.
4. issue_ordinal is one-based per input issue and shared by its copies. run_copies is cumulative requested copies through the current input.
5. Copy title unchanged. copies_text is the decimal text of copies.

Current transform:
```ctl
//#CTL2
integer issueCount;
long requestedCopies;
date previousIssue;
boolean regression;
function integer count() {
 regression = $in.0.issued_at < previousIssue;
 if ($in.0.copies > 1) previousIssue = $in.0.issued_at;
 issueCount++;
 requestedCopies = requestedCopies + $in.0.copies;
 return $in.0.copies;
}
function integer transform(integer idx) {
 $out.0.title = $in.0.title;
 $out.0.copy_number = idx + 1;
 $out.0.issue_ordinal = issueCount + 1;
 $out.0.copies_text = num2string($in.0.copies);
 $out.0.regressed = regression;
 $out.0.active = $in.0.cancelled_at == null;
 $out.0.held = $in.0.hold_until > $in.0.issued_at;
 $out.0.run_copies = requestedCopies;
 return ALL;
}
```

